{"skill":{"slug":"trading-coach","displayName":"Trading Coach"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770007898748,"changelog":"Initial release of Trading Coach — an AI-powered trading review tool.\n\n- Automatically imports and matches trading records from major Chinese brokerages (Futu, Tiger, CITIC, Huatai, etc.).\n- Generates professional-grade review reports and actionable improvement insights based on broker CSV files.\n- Provides 8-dimension position scoring (entry/exit/trend/risk/behavior/news/execution...)\n- Delivers 10-dimension AI-powered trading analysis, highlighting patterns and areas for improvement.\n- Supports quickstart CLI workflow and detailed scoring/insight documentation.\n- Outputs clear summaries of trading statistics and personalized recommendations.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3636,"sha256":"985ac333d195b654a6a8c450a0cfed7d69fefed57e7e7f36a14c540349f5f569","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/csv_formats.md","size":3659,"sha256":"cb8f5220d7c964865bb72e799683337537813898b935c8b32a7508424342e72c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/insight_dimensions.md","size":5318,"sha256":"4d8987b1e7205b2092db439a5edabd7fb8cb3f65bc380775b2cda88cfbf92a9e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/scoring_system.md","size":5233,"sha256":"a8d778a393c278abd5d3f8dc3bc721bd7104126683fcaaba598a19ed5bbc0b5e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2152,"sha256":"f64b27b911981c78e43bd4f7e7e9f203af4e62bdb25dfa56d317a2b7307b47bb","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789027830797,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a49ba942890004e0208adf78c0ed68330f0c927cba91421ff9df4e742bef926a","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a49ba942890004e0208adf78c0ed68330f0c927cba91421ff9df4e742bef926a","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: trading-coach\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe SKILL.md file instructs the AI agent to `git clone` an external GitHub repository (`https://github.com/BENZEMA216/tradingcoach.git`) and subsequently execute Python scripts and install dependencies (`pip install -r requirements.txt`) from the downloaded content. This introduces a significant supply chain risk, as the actual code being executed is fetched from an external, unverified source not included in the bundle. While the stated purpose of the skill is benign trading analysis, the instruction to download and execute arbitrary external code is a high-risk capability.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160813542},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":26,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789027830797},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This trading-analysis skill is not overtly malicious, but it asks users to run unreviewed remote code on sensitive brokerage files.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Running downloaded Python scripts and pip installs in a venv is purpose-related but not contained; the scripts would execute with the user's normal local file and network access while handling brokerage CSV data.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The quick start clones a mutable external GitHub repository, installs its requirements, and runs scripts that are not included in the reviewed artifact, with no pinned commit, signature, checksum, lockfile, or hash verification.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The trigger text includes broad phrases such as general trade analysis or review requests, and the skill does not require explicit confirmation before processing brokerage records.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The artifact creates a persistent local checkout, virtual environment, and config file in the user's home directory, but I found no scheduled task, startup hook, credential theft instruction, privilege escalation, or destructive behavior in the reviewed files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: import brokerage CSVs, pair trades, score positions, and generate trading review insights. The capability necessarily involves sensitive financial trading records.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable running code from the referenced GitHub repository after reviewing it yourself. Prefer pinning a known commit, reviewing requirements, running it in an isolated environment, and redacting account identifiers or unnecessary personal fields from brokerage exports before use.","findings":"[T03] unexpected: Accepted as a material review concern: the artifact's install instructions depend on unpinned remote code and dependencies outside the audited package, then run that code on sensitive financial CSVs.\n[SQP-2] expected: Processing brokerage CSVs is central to the skill, but the artifact under-discloses privacy, redaction, retention, and handling expectations for sensitive financial records.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad activation phrases are not necessary for the purpose and could bring the skill into ordinary trading-analysis requests without a clear opt-in to process records.\n[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-language references are coherent with the supported Chinese brokerage formats and audience; this is a usability/localization note rather than a security concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789027830797}}}}}